+{"created_at": "2026-07-01T00:07:42.033408+00:00", "ocr_backend": "sglang", "ocr_endpoint_version": "modal-sglang-unlimited-ocr-v1", "ocr_model": "Unlimited-OCR", "ocr_model_version": "Unlimited-OCR", "ocr_text": "<PAGE><|det|>header [72, 56, 211, 72]<|/det|>LYSWP2-8\n<|det|>title [72, 97, 818, 190]<|/det|>UNCHECKED ERC2O TRANSFER\nRETURN VALUE MAY CAUSE HTLC\nINCONSISTENCY ACROSS CHAINS\n<|det|>text [73, 222, 207, 243]<|/det|>SEVERITY:\n<|det|>text [291, 223, 388, 242]<|/det|>Medium\n<|det|>text [72, 276, 152, 294]<|/det|>PATH:\n<|det|>text [71, 311, 858, 350]<|/det|>chains/starknet/src/HashTimeLockedERC20.cairo#L391-L464, HashTimeLockedERC20.cairo#L339, HashTimeLockedERC20.cairo#L423\n<|det|>title [72, 370, 259, 390]<|/det|>REMEDIATION:\n<|det|>text [71, 405, 832, 466]<|/det|>Explicitly check all ERC20 transfer return values (transferFrom[] and transfer[]). If the function returns false, the transaction should revert immediately.\n<|det|>text [73, 498, 168, 518]<|/det|>STATUS:\n<|det|>text [238, 500, 303, 517]<|/det|>Fixed\n<|det|>title [72, 551, 259, 570]<|/det|>DESCRIPTION:\n<|det|>text [71, 585, 909, 723]<|/det|>The contract does not check the return value of transferFrom[] and transfer[] in multiple places, assuming that all ERC20 transfers will succeed. This is an issue because some ERC20 tokens do not revert on failure but instead return false. If the contract does not explicitly validate these return values, it may proceed with logic without actually transferring the funds, leading to severe inconsistencies.\n<|det|>text [71, 735, 911, 873]<|/det|>The commit[] function executes an ERC20 transferFrom[] call to move tokens from the user to the contract. However, the function does not check the return value of transferFrom[], assuming it will always succeed. In cases where the ERC20 token does not revert on failure but instead returns false, the function will continue execution without actually transferring funds.\n<|det|>page_number [911, 956, 937, 970]<|/de